{"id":"S0183","name":"Tor","description":"Tor is a software suite and network that provides increased anonymity on the Internet. It creates a multi-hop proxy network and utilizes multilayer encryption to protect both the message and routing information. Tor utilizes \"Onion Routing,\" in which messages are encrypted with multiple layers of encryption; at each step in the proxy network, the topmost layer is decrypted and the contents forwarded on to the next node until it reaches its destination.","kind":"attack_tool","upstream_type":"tool","stix_id":"tool--ed7d0cb1-87a6-43b4-9f46-ef1bc56d6c68","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.741Z","aliases":["Tor"],"platforms":["Linux","Windows","macOS"],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0183","source_domains":["enterprise"],"classification_note":"Included because the active pinned ATT&CK object has type tool. This is an upstream classification, not an assurance of benignness or a recommendation to run it.","page":"tools/S0183/","reviewed_on":"2026-09-27","guides":[],"guide_currentness":"Historical guides retain publication dates. Commands and product availability have not been revalidated.","techniques":[{"key":"enterprise/T1090.003","id":"T1090.003","name":"Multi-hop Proxy","domain":"enterprise","page":"techniques/enterprise/T1090.003/","environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--92e4cc06-5708-4486-92cc-0d25d9a755d4","description":"Traffic traversing the Tor network will be forwarded to multiple nodes before exiting the Tor network and continuing on to its intended destination.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0183","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0004","name":"Firmware Modification","tag":"Firmware Modification","p